WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.880
I have a very vivid memory

00:00:02.920 --> 00:00:06.760
of my GP saying to me:

00:00:06.800 --> 00:00:08.880
"You are mentally sick

00:00:08.920 --> 00:00:11.800
and you have to accept help
to get better."

00:00:11.840 --> 00:00:15.240
Hannah was a healthy
20-year-old psychology student

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:16.920
living at home with her family

00:00:16.960 --> 00:00:19.920
when she started experiencing
flu-like symptoms.

00:00:25.480 --> 00:00:27.760
I went to my GP
and I was kind of told

00:00:27.800 --> 00:00:29.560
that viruses
will just generally go,

00:00:29.600 --> 00:00:31.960
you just need to go home
and rest, take it easy.

00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:34.240
Her GP thought
she had glandular fever.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:38.040
Hannah was feeling very tired,
so the symptoms fitted.

00:00:38.080 --> 00:00:40.240
But then she started
to develop changes

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:41.280
in her personality.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:44.720
Soon after, Hannah lost
her ability to speak.

00:00:44.760 --> 00:00:46.640
I had to ask my mum
to come in,

00:00:46.680 --> 00:00:50.080
sit with me
and talk for me to the GP.

00:00:50.120 --> 00:00:51.920
I would kind of write down
to my mum

00:00:51.960 --> 00:00:53.200
what needed to be said.

00:00:53.240 --> 00:00:55.680
Hannah was sent home
with antidepressants

00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:57.880
and a referral
to a psychologist.

00:00:57.920 --> 00:01:00.960
Her symptoms deteriorated,
and she was soon admitted

00:01:01.000 --> 00:01:02.360
to a psychiatric hospital,

00:01:02.400 --> 00:01:05.120
where she was given
antipsychotic medication.

00:01:05.160 --> 00:01:06.720
She was seen by a psychiatrist,

00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:08.760
who ordered an MRI scan.

00:01:08.800 --> 00:01:11.720
During the scan, doctors found
a cyst on her brain

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:13.880
and sent her to A&amp;E
for investigation.

00:01:13.920 --> 00:01:14.960
When I got to A&amp;E,

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:16.680
they reviewed the cyst

00:01:16.720 --> 00:01:18.400
and said
I was probably born with it,

00:01:18.440 --> 00:01:20.600
it probably had nothing to do
with the symptoms.

00:01:20.640 --> 00:01:22.240
But what they did notice was

00:01:22.280 --> 00:01:24.040
that my blood test showed
I was fighting

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.200
some sort of virus.

00:01:25.240 --> 00:01:26.480
More tests followed,

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:28.880
and after three weeks,
the results came back,

00:01:28.920 --> 00:01:30.760
and Hannah finally got
her diagnosis:

00:01:30.800 --> 00:01:35.280
Anti-NMDA receptor
encephalitis.

00:01:35.320 --> 00:01:38.120
It's an autoimmune form
of encephalitis,

00:01:38.160 --> 00:01:40.040
which is the inflammation
of the brain.

00:01:40.080 --> 00:01:43.040
According to
Professor Guy Leschziner,

00:01:43.080 --> 00:01:46.000
having your physical symptoms
mistaken for a mental illness

00:01:46.040 --> 00:01:47.560
is not uncommon.

00:01:47.600 --> 00:01:49.320
We do occasionally
see individuals

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:51.680
with very severe psychosis
and behavioural change

00:01:51.720 --> 00:01:53.960
in whom the initial diagnosis

00:01:54.000 --> 00:01:57.880
is of a psychotic illness
like schizophrenia.

00:01:57.920 --> 00:01:59.200
But actually,

00:01:59.240 --> 00:02:01.120
over the course of days
or weeks

00:02:01.160 --> 00:02:02.680
whilst they're in hospital,

00:02:02.720 --> 00:02:04.760
it begins to be obvious
that actually

00:02:04.800 --> 00:02:06.880
what is underlying
their condition

00:02:06.920 --> 00:02:08.800
is one of these
autoimmune conditions.

00:02:08.840 --> 00:02:10.960
It's been known
for more than a century

00:02:11.000 --> 00:02:13.640
that damage to particular parts
of the brain

00:02:13.680 --> 00:02:16.120
and things like tumours
can result in changes

00:02:16.160 --> 00:02:17.960
in personality or behaviour.

00:02:18.000 --> 00:02:20.480
But over
the last 20 years or so,

00:02:20.520 --> 00:02:22.000
we've begun to recognise

00:02:22.040 --> 00:02:23.960
that there are a number
of conditions

00:02:24.000 --> 00:02:26.320
that have an immune basis,

00:02:26.360 --> 00:02:29.840
whereby the immune system
attacks the brain

00:02:29.880 --> 00:02:31.480
and causes changes

00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:32.760
to the functioning
of that brain.

00:02:32.800 --> 00:02:33.960
In Hannah's case,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:37.320
it took several weeks
for doctors to recognise

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.920
that this was a serious
autoimmune condition

00:02:39.960 --> 00:02:42.880
that required treatment
with very heavy-duty drugs.

00:02:42.920 --> 00:02:44.640
I was moved
to neurology ward.

00:02:44.680 --> 00:02:46.800
I was completely mute

00:02:46.840 --> 00:02:51.160
and I had lost the ability
to dress myself,

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.360
wash myself, feed myself.

00:02:53.400 --> 00:02:57.080
So I really was trapped
in my own body at this stage.

00:02:57.120 --> 00:02:59.600
Hannah underwent
immunotherapy treatment

00:02:59.640 --> 00:03:01.960
and had 13 plasma exchanges –

00:03:02.000 --> 00:03:03.920
a process of filtering blood

00:03:03.960 --> 00:03:06.480
before pumping it
back into her body.

00:03:06.520 --> 00:03:08.320
Although the treatment
didn't work initially,

00:03:08.360 --> 00:03:10.240
and her parents were told
by doctors

00:03:10.280 --> 00:03:11.920
she probably didn't have
long to live,

00:03:11.960 --> 00:03:13.800
after two weeks,
Hannah woke up.

00:03:13.840 --> 00:03:17.400
Hannah, say "Dad".

00:03:17.440 --> 00:03:18.920
Dad.

00:03:18.960 --> 00:03:20.520
Over subsequent weeks,

00:03:20.560 --> 00:03:23.520
she learnt to speak again
and walk again.

00:03:23.560 --> 00:03:25.840
She says it was like learning
how to live again.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:27.640
I look back at the person

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:29.160
before I got encephalitis,

00:03:29.200 --> 00:03:30.680
and I don't really know her.

00:03:32.200 --> 00:03:34.120
I just can't connect
with that person.

00:03:34.160 --> 00:03:37.400
Five years on,
Hannah has mostly recovered,

00:03:37.440 --> 00:03:39.880
though she is still
on immunotherapy treatment,

00:03:39.920 --> 00:03:42.480
and that makes her
more vulnerable to infections

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:44.840
and could impact her fertility.

00:03:44.880 --> 00:03:48.400
I wish GPs would know
more about encephalitis,

00:03:48.440 --> 00:03:50.440
because they're the first point
of contact

00:03:50.480 --> 00:03:51.960
for a lot of patients.

00:03:52.000 --> 00:03:54.480
I wish my GP knew
more about it,

00:03:54.520 --> 00:03:57.440
so she could direct me
to the right pathway.

00:03:57.480 --> 00:04:00.680
If I was to think about all
the people who had encephalitis

00:04:00.720 --> 00:04:03.120
and died
in psychiatric hospitals

00:04:03.160 --> 00:04:04.240
or care homes,

00:04:04.280 --> 00:04:06.520
I wouldn't be able to sleep
at night.

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:07.800
In Hannah's case,

00:04:07.840 --> 00:04:11.400
a physical illness,
encephalitis, was mistaken

00:04:11.440 --> 00:04:12.960
for mental illness.

00:04:13.000 --> 00:04:15.400
But sometimes
it's the other way around.

00:04:15.440 --> 00:04:17.080
We know that the connection

00:04:17.120 --> 00:04:19.320
between body and mind
goes both ways.

00:04:19.360 --> 00:04:23.920
Physical problems can result
in psychiatric symptoms,

00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:26.560
but also psychological issues

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:28.640
can contribute
to physical disease.

00:04:28.680 --> 00:04:31.600
Professor Leschziner
says he sees patients

00:04:31.640 --> 00:04:34.000
who have symptoms
like seizures, paralysis

00:04:34.040 --> 00:04:37.440
and numbness
with no obvious physical cause.

00:04:37.480 --> 00:04:39.640
Some are eventually diagnosed

00:04:39.680 --> 00:04:41.680
as having functional
neurological disorder,

00:04:41.720 --> 00:04:42.920
or FND,

00:04:42.960 --> 00:04:45.000
which is a problem
with how the brain receives

00:04:45.040 --> 00:04:47.000
and sends information
to the rest of the body.

00:04:47.040 --> 00:04:49.040
We don't fully understand

00:04:49.080 --> 00:04:50.320
what causes these conditions.

00:04:50.360 --> 00:04:52.680
It seems that anybody
can be vulnerable to changes

00:04:52.720 --> 00:04:54.880
within the software
that defines

00:04:54.920 --> 00:04:56.880
how our nervous systems work.

00:04:56.920 --> 00:04:59.760
We know that there are
some risk factors.

00:04:59.800 --> 00:05:03.000
So stress, anxiety, depression,

00:05:03.040 --> 00:05:05.760
previous psychological trauma
in particular.

00:05:05.800 --> 00:05:07.040
But ultimately,

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:08.200
anybody can develop

00:05:08.240 --> 00:05:10.160
these functional
neurological disorders.

00:05:10.200 --> 00:05:13.000
Globally,
hundreds of thousands of people

00:05:13.040 --> 00:05:15.120
develop FND every year.

00:05:15.160 --> 00:05:17.280
Conditions like FND

00:05:17.320 --> 00:05:19.680
and the experiences of people
like Hannah

00:05:19.720 --> 00:05:22.240
have led some doctors
to believe that we need

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:24.320
to stop thinking
of mental and physical health

00:05:24.360 --> 00:05:25.640
as separate.

00:05:25.680 --> 00:05:27.320
I think we need to move away

00:05:27.360 --> 00:05:30.640
from defining diseases
or disorders

00:05:30.680 --> 00:05:33.440
as of the body and of the mind.

00:05:33.480 --> 00:05:36.880
We know that actually,
in almost all cases,

00:05:36.920 --> 00:05:38.960
there are contributions
from both.

00:05:39.000 --> 00:05:40.920
Even in conditions
that are thought to have

00:05:40.960 --> 00:05:43.240
a pure physical basis,

00:05:43.280 --> 00:05:45.720
we know that how people
interpret their symptoms

00:05:45.760 --> 00:05:49.040
is important in terms of
defining their quality of life

00:05:49.080 --> 00:05:51.880
and how severe they perceive
their symptoms to be.

00:05:51.920 --> 00:05:54.000
So actually understanding that,

00:05:54.040 --> 00:05:56.760
making sure
that everybody has access

00:05:56.800 --> 00:05:59.320
to both physical
and psychological treatments

00:05:59.360 --> 00:06:01.120
is really of utmost importance

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:04.280
for pretty much every condition
that is seen

00:06:04.320 --> 00:06:05.800
by our healthcare systems,

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:07.720
and is important for everyone.

